From c626d6a4d1f0de4792c838dc9ae71eab3dbd9600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:34:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 136/274] Adaptive verification: run the draft budget eagerly;
 report torch.compile in serving

The draft-budget selection was a torch.compile function, first compiled on the
first step that trims a budget: the second decode step of the first request
after a boot. Inductor's launcher then loaded its kernels with cuModuleLoad,
which holds the GIL while it waits for the device. The device was waiting for
the asynchronous disk Engram rows, whose reader thread needs the GIL, so the
workers hung; a rank that escaped ran alone into the next collective
(spark-ds41f experiments/2026-10-15-engram-stall).

Run the selection eagerly (six small ops: no compilation and no lazily loaded
module) and load its kernels at startup, after the cost profile. The JIT monitor
now reports torch.compile compilations during inference, which its Triton hook
misses when the compile cache serves the kernels.

